---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Why Buildprints — architecture slides for coding agents"
  description="A kinetic slide deck explaining Agent Buildprint: exact architecture packages coding agents can bootstrap, follow, and validate."
>
  <main class="why-deck" aria-label="Why Agent Buildprint cinematic slide deck">
    <nav class="deck-rail" aria-label="Slide navigation">
      <a href="#slide-hero"><span>00</span>Open</a>
      <a href="#slide-chaos"><span>01</span>Chaos</a>
      <a href="#slide-blueprint"><span>02</span>Blueprint</a>
      <a href="#slide-package"><span>03</span>Package</a>
      <a href="#slide-flow"><span>04</span>Flow</a>
      <a href="#slide-proof"><span>05</span>Proof</a>
      <a href="#slide-market"><span>06</span>Market</a>
    </nav>

    <section id="slide-hero" class="why-slide hero-slide" aria-labelledby="why-title">
      <div class="slide-copy">
        <p class="deck-kicker">Agent Buildprint / cinematic deck</p>
        <h1 id="why-title">Architecture that agents can actually follow.</h1>
        <p class="deck-lead">A Buildprint is not another prompt. It is a verified construction sequence: exact docs, scope rails, contracts, tests, and proof gates.</p>
        <div class="why-actions">
          <a class="btn primary" href="/buildprints/">Browse Buildprints</a>
          <a class="btn" href="#slide-chaos">Play the story ↓</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="orbital-stage" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="blueprint-core">BUILD<br/>PRINT</div>
        <span style="--i:0">SPEC</span>
        <span style="--i:1">PLAN</span>
        <span style="--i:2">TEST</span>
        <span style="--i:3">PROOF</span>
        <span style="--i:4">SCOPE</span>
        <span style="--i:5">TRACE</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="slide-chaos" class="why-slide chaos-slide">
      <div class="slide-copy">
        <p class="slide-number">01 / The failure mode</p>
        <h2>Agents are fast enough to build the wrong thing beautifully.</h2>
        <p>Without a reusable architecture contract, the model fills gaps with confidence: guessed components, mushy scope, late tests, fake parity, and “done” from one happy path.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chaos-board" aria-label="Uncontrolled agent drift graphic">
        <div class="prompt-chip">“Build me a RAG app”</div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 520 380" role="img" aria-label="Drift lines from prompt to bad outcomes">
          <path d="M72 92 C180 42 238 150 338 70 S470 82 474 32" />
          <path d="M70 145 C176 245 242 94 350 184 S462 260 492 150" />
          <path d="M72 214 C180 174 246 310 356 260 S452 272 486 338" />
          <path d="M82 282 C176 330 252 206 358 312 S438 188 486 236" />
        </svg>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Scope creep</b><span>quietly expands</span></li>
          <li><b>Architecture drift</b><span>changes mid-build</span></li>
          <li><b>Validation theatre</b><span>tests after code</span></li>
          <li><b>Parity overclaim</b><span>demo ≠ product</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="slide-blueprint" class="why-slide blueprint-slide">
      <div class="stamp-cloud" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>NO VIBES</span><span>EXACT SNAPSHOTS</span><span>CLAIM BOUNDARY</span><span>RUN THE GATE</span>
      </div>
      <div class="slide-copy wide">
        <p class="slide-number">02 / The intervention</p>
        <h2>Give the agent the senior-engineer thinking before it touches files.</h2>
        <p>Buildprints convert repeated product architecture into a portable packet the agent can bootstrap, inspect, execute, and validate.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="slide-package" class="why-slide package-slide">
      <div class="slide-copy">
        <p class="slide-number">03 / The object</p>
        <h2>A Buildprint is a stack of executable decisions.</h2>
        <p>Every file has a job. The agent does not scrape marketing cards or invent missing architecture.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="file-cascade" aria-label="Buildprint package files">
        <article><b>BUILDPRINT.md</b><span>architecture truth</span></article>
        <article><b>SPEC.md</b><span>behavior contract</span></article>
        <article><b>PLAN.md</b><span>ordered implementation rails</span></article>
        <article><b>CONTRACTS.md</b><span>interfaces, data, events</span></article>
        <article><b>TEST_MATRIX.md</b><span>risk → proof gates</span></article>
        <article><b>VALIDATION_REPORT.md</b><span>evidence, not vibes</span></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="slide-flow" class="why-slide flow-slide">
      <p class="slide-number">04 / The machine</p>
      <h2>The agent moves through a constrained build tunnel.</h2>
      <div class="flow-machine" aria-label="Buildprint execution flow">
        <div><span>01</span><b>Choose</b><small>architecture</small></div>
        <i></i>
        <div><span>02</span><b>Bootstrap</b><small><code>agb start</code></small></div>
        <i></i>
        <div><span>03</span><b>Build</b><small>from snapshots</small></div>
        <i></i>
        <div><span>04</span><b>Validate</b><small>tests + proof</small></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="slide-proof" class="why-slide proof-slide">
      <div class="slide-copy">
        <p class="slide-number">05 / The trust layer</p>
        <h2>“Done” has to leave evidence.</h2>
        <p>Validated Buildprints carry runnable proof: build logs, test counts, raw file checks, bootstrap checks, and explicit claim boundaries.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-terminal" aria-label="Validation terminal graphic">
        <p><span>$</span> agb start package.json</p>
        <p class="ok">✓ downloaded exact snapshots</p>
        <p><span>$</span> npm test</p>
        <p class="ok">✓ 12/12 proof tests passed</p>
        <p><span>$</span> check claims</p>
        <p class="warn">! clone/API/provider parity excluded</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="slide-market" class="why-slide market-slide">
      <div class="slide-copy wide">
        <p class="slide-number">06 / The category</p>
        <h2>Docker Hub for environments. npm for code. Buildprints for agent architecture.</h2>
        <p>Build new systems, map real products into clean-room blueprints, and benchmark agents on the same architecture task.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="poster-grid" aria-label="Agent Buildprint use cases">
        <article><span>Build</span><b>RAG, billing, agents, content OS</b></article>
        <article><span>Map</span><b>GitHub products into clean-room architecture</b></article>
        <article><span>Benchmark</span><b>Codex vs Claude vs Cursor on one task</b></article>
      </div>
      <div class="why-actions final-actions">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/buildprints/">Browse Buildprints</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/buildprints/superpowers-skill-methodology-harness/">See Superpowers Harness</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
